# DBW LEAD SYSTEM — UNIVERSAL RULES

## HARD STOP RULES
These apply to every rep, every run, no exceptions.
If any tool fails twice in a row: skip that lead
and move to the next. Do not retry endlessly.
If runtime hits 15 minutes: stop, log shortfall, done.
Never fabricate company names, contacts, or numbers.
Never duplicate a company delivered in a previous run.

## SAGE COMPLIANCE RULES
Print the full Sage compliance block on every single
lead card without exception. These rules govern
whether a rep can work a lead and what commission
rate applies. They are non-negotiable.

RULE 1 — Cross-reference in Sage before any call.
Not optional. No exceptions ever.

RULE 2 — Active Account (invoice within 18 months):
Lead is NOT available to this rep. Pass the full
lead card immediately to the rep who currently owns
this account in Sage. Do not call. Do not prospect.

RULE 3 — Reactivation (invoice 18 to 36 months ago):
Lead is fair game to prospect. Does NOT qualify for
the new account commission rate of 25%. Standard
commission rates apply until 36 full months have
passed since the last invoice date.

RULE 4 — New Account (36+ months or never invoiced):
Fully fair game. Qualifies for the new account
commission rate of 25% upon first sale.

## COMPANY SIZE FILTER
Sweet spot: 2-500 employees, $1M-$20M revenue.
Must have crews actively on site using saws and blades.
Self-performing only. Skip subcontracting-only firms.

## WHO TO TARGET
Fill all 5 leads from Primary targets first. Move to
Secondary only if Primary cannot fill all 5 slots.
Use Low Priority only as an absolute last resort.

Primary — always pull from here first:
Concrete contractors, roadway and DOT contractors,
curb and gutter crews, bridge contractors, airport
and runway contractors, commercial concrete crews
that are self-performing, asphalt and paving
contractors, masonry contractors, site work
contractors, utility and underground contractors,
demolition contractors.

Secondary — fill remaining slots if Primary is short:
Core drilling companies.

Low Priority — use only to fill a gap when Primary
and Secondary together cannot reach 5 leads:
Professional concrete cutting and sawing specialty
firms. These contacts negotiate extremely hard,
frequently return product, and routinely give reps
a difficult time after the sale. Never first choice.

Auto-skip under all circumstances:
GCs who subcontract all field work, architects,
engineers, supply houses, equipment rental companies,
developers, and consultants. If they do not have
guys on site running saws, skip them without
exception.

## SOURCE WATERFALL ORDER
Work through sources in this exact order for every
rep. Move to the next source only when the current
one returns fewer than 5 qualified results.

SOURCE 1 — ZoomInfo (always start here):
Use the ZoomInfo connector. Call Search Companies.
NAICS codes: 238140, 237310, 238110.
Location: the rep's assigned city cluster for today.
Size filter: 2-500 employees.
Pull 8-10 candidates to allow for disqualification.
Extract all available company data before moving on.

SOURCE 2 — ConstructConnect:
Pull active or recently awarded projects in territory.
Extract every bidding subcontractor from each project.
Each bidder is a potential lead candidate.

SOURCE 3 — Tango:
Search DOT and government awarded contracts in
territory. Pull all active contractor names found.

SOURCE 4 — Free web (last resort only):
Use only if Sources 1 through 3 combined have not
produced 5 qualified leads. Search using any
combination of Google, LinkedIn company search,
Facebook and Instagram business pages showing active
jobsite work, Manta.com, BBB.org, and Bluebook.com.

## CONTACT ENRICHMENT RULES
Run dbw-contact-enrichment.skill for every company.
ZoomInfo Enrich Contacts and Enrich Scoops are always
the first calls. Mobile number from ZoomInfo is always
the priority contact number.
Find between 1 and 5 contacts per company.
Contact priority order: Owner or President or Partner
first, then Superintendent or Site Super or Shop
Manager, then Operations Manager or VP Operations,
then Project Manager, then Foreman as last resort.
If no verified contact with a real phone number is
found after exhausting all fallback sources:
disqualify that lead and replace it. No placeholders.
No guessed numbers. No fabricated data. Ever.

## DELIVERY RULES
The Gmail draft must be fully formatted HTML.
Do not deliver plain text under any circumstances.
One Gmail draft per rep per day to jfgreco84@gmail.com
Run lead-card-format.skill to build the HTML output.
Do not send the email. Create the draft only.
After the Gmail draft is created: STOP. Task complete.

